.TH GIT\-ARCHIVE 1 "2026-10-30" "git-archive 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git\-archive \- clone, update and verify archives of git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git\-archive
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ SOURCE ...]
.br
.B git\-archive
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git\-archive
maintains a directory of git repositories collected from
.IR sources :
whole organizations, users and groups on GitHub, GitLab and Gitea/Forgejo,
or single repositories on any git server.
The first run clones everything; later runs fetch what changed.
Work runs in parallel with live progress.
.PP
An archive never loses data on its own.
Repositories deleted upstream are kept and flagged as
.IR gone .
Branches and tags that upstream force\-pushes, moves or deletes are
preserved under
.I refs/archive/
before they are replaced.
Excluded repositories stay on disk but are no longer updated.
.PP
Note that
.B git archive
(with a space) is an unrelated built\-in git command; invoke this
program as
.BR git\-archive .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR sync " [" \fISOURCE\fR ...]
The default command.
Adds the given sources (creating the archive if needed), then clones new
and updates existing repositories.
Without sources it updates the archive.
.TP
.BI add " SOURCE" ...
Adds sources, or updates the options of existing ones, without syncing.
.TP
.BI remove " SOURCE" ...
Forgets sources (alias
.BR rm ).
Their repositories stay on disk and are listed as
.IR orphaned .
.TP
.BI exclude " PATTERN" ...
Stops cloning and updating matching repositories.
.TP
.BI include " PATTERN" ...
Removes an exclusion.
If a broader pattern still excludes matching repositories, a negated
pattern
.RI ( !PATTERN )
is added.
.TP
.BR list " [" \fIPATTERN\fR ...]
Lists repositories and their status without network access
(aliases
.BR ls ,
.BR status ).
Statuses: ok, failed, corrupt, missing, pending, gone, excluded,
filtered, orphaned, unmanaged, absent.
With
.BR \-\-sources ,
lists the configured sources instead.
.TP
.BR verify " [" \fIPATTERN\fR ...]
Checks every repository with
.BR "git fsck \-\-strict" ,
verifies its remote URL and HEAD, and reports modified working trees.
.TP
.BR gc " [" \fIPATTERN\fR ...]
Runs
.B git gc
on repositories in parallel and removes leftovers of interrupted clones.
.TP
.BR config " [" \fIGIT\-CONFIG\-ARGS\fR ...]
Runs
.B git config \-\-file .git\-archive/config
with the given arguments (default
.BR \-\-list ;
.B \-\-edit
opens the file in an editor) and validates the result.
.TP
.BI completion " SHELL"
Prints a completion script for
.BR bash ,
.B zsh
or
.BR fish .
.TP
.BR help " [" \fICOMMAND\fR "], " version
Show help or the version.
.SH SOURCES
.TP
.B https://github.com/termux
All repositories of an organization or user.
.B http://
URLs of known forges are upgraded to
.BR https:// .
.TP
.B https://github.com/termux/termux\-app
A single repository.
.TP
.B \-\-provider github termux
The same as an owner URL on the provider's public instance
(github.com, gitlab.com, codeberg.org).
.TP
.B https://gitlab.com/group/subgroup
A GitLab group (including subgroups), user or project.
.TP
.B https://codeberg.org/forgejo
A Gitea or Forgejo owner or repository.
Self\-hosted instances are recognized by host names starting with
.BR gitlab. ,
.B gitea.
or
.BR forgejo. ,
or need
.BR \-\-provider .
.TP
.BR git@host:owner/repo.git ", " ssh://... ", " https://host/path/repo.git
Any git repository.
Local repositories may be given as a path or
.B file://
URL.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global options
.TP
.BI \-C ", " \-\-archive\-dir " DIR"
Archive location.
Defaults to
.B $GIT_ARCHIVE_DIR
or the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only errors and warnings; suitable for cron.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also report unchanged and skipped repositories.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
.BR auto " (default), " always " or " never .
.B NO_COLOR
is honoured.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version
.SS Options of sync, verify and gc
.TP
.BI \-j ", " \-\-jobs " N"
Repositories processed in parallel (default: archive.jobs, 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Abort a git command that produces no output for this long
(default: archive.timeout, 10m).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a machine\-readable report on standard output.
.SS Options of sync and add
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-provider " NAME"
Provider of the following sources:
.BR github ", " gitlab ", " gitea " or " git .
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-forks ", " \-\-skip\-archived
Do not archive forks or repositories archived upstream.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-size " SIZE"
Skip repositories larger than
.I SIZE
(e.g.
.BR 2G )
as reported by the API.
.TP
.B \-\-wiki
Also archive wiki repositories.
.TP
.B \-\-lfs
Also fetch Git LFS objects (requires git\-lfs).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preserve
Do not keep history rewritten upstream under
.IR refs/archive/ .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-metadata
Do not save metadata snapshots.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh
Clone over ssh instead of https.
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-env " VAR"
Environment variable that holds an access token for these sources.
.TP
.BI \-\-api " URL"
API base URL for instances at a non\-standard location.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Allow unencrypted
.B http://
and
.B git://
sources.
.TP
.BI \-x ", " \-\-exclude " PATTERN"
Exclude matching repositories.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " LAYOUT"
For a new archive:
.B worktree
(default; a checked\-out default branch) or
.B bare
(no working tree; smaller, and nothing from the repositories is
written as files).
.TP
.B \-\-init
Allow creating an archive in a non\-empty directory.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-only " PATTERN"
(sync) Process only matching repositories.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
(sync) Show what would be cloned, updated and skipped; change nothing.
.SS Options of verify and gc
.TP
.B \-\-quick
(verify) Check connectivity only; much faster.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote
(verify) Compare local refs with upstream using
.BR "git ls\-remote" ;
nothing is downloaded.
.TP
.B \-\-aggressive
(gc) Pass
.B \-\-aggressive
to
.BR "git gc" .
.SH PATTERNS
Patterns select repositories by ID,
.IR host/owner/repo .
Each slash\-separated part is a shell glob
.RB ( * ", " ? ", " [...] );
.B **
spans parts.
A pattern may match any contiguous part of the ID, so
.BR termux\-packages ,
.B termux/termux\-packages
and
.B github.com/termux/termux\-packages
select the same repository, and
.B github.com/termux
selects everything below it.
A leading
.B /
anchors at the host.
In the exclusion list,
.B !PATTERN
re\-includes and the last matching pattern decides.
Wikis follow their repository.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I .git\-archive/config
uses
.BR git\-config (1)
syntax and may be edited by hand; comments are preserved.
.SS [archive]
.TP
.B layout
.BR worktree " or " bare ;
fixed at creation.
.TP
.BR jobs ", " timeout ", " retries
Parallelism (4), inactivity timeout (10m), retries of transient
network failures (2).
.TP
.B exclude
Exclusion pattern; repeatable.
.PP
Any per\-source option below may also be set in
.B [archive]
as the default for all sources.
.SS [source "NAME"]
.TP
.BR url ", " provider ", " type
Where the source lives;
.B type
is
.B owner
or
.BR repo .
.TP
.BR api ", " insecure ", " tokenEnv
As the corresponding options.
.TP
.BR skipForks ", " skipArchived ", " maxSize ", " wiki ", " lfs
Selection options (defaults: false, false, unlimited, false, false).
.TP
.BR metadata ", " preserve
Metadata snapshots and preservation of rewritten refs (default: true).
.TP
.B protocol
.B https
(default) or
.BR ssh .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <archive>/<host>/<owner>/<repo>
Repositories (with a
.B .git
suffix in the bare layout).
.TP
.I <archive>/.git\-archive/config
Configuration.
.TP
.I <archive>/.git\-archive/state.json
Bookkeeping (sync and verify results, forge IDs, gone dates).
Rebuilt automatically if lost or damaged.
.TP
.I <archive>/.git\-archive/metadata/<host>/<owner>/<repo>.json
Metadata snapshots: description, topics, license, stars, dates.
.TP
.I <archive>/.git\-archive/lock
Prevents concurrent modifying runs.
.TP
.I <repo>/refs/archive/<UTC\-time>/{heads,tags,local}/<name>
Tips that upstream rewrote or deleted, and local commits that a
checkout would have orphaned.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_ARCHIVE_DIR
Default archive location.
.TP
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN ", " GH_TOKEN
Token for github.com.
.TP
.B GITLAB_TOKEN
Token for gitlab.com.
.TP
.BR CODEBERG_TOKEN ", " GITEA_TOKEN
Token for codeberg.org.
.PP
These variables are used only for the public instances they belong to;
self\-hosted sources name their variable with
.BR \-\-token\-env .
Tokens are never written to disk.
.SH SECURITY
Repository content, forge API responses and server messages are
treated as hostile:
.IP \(bu 2
Names from APIs are validated before they become paths (no
.BR .. ,
.BR .git ,
separators or leading dashes); repositories outside the requested
owner are ignored; clone URLs are built locally instead of being taken
from API responses.
.IP \(bu 2
git runs with configuration that cannot be overridden by repositories
or user files: hooks and fsmonitor disabled,
.B transfer.fsckObjects
(malicious trees are rejected before they are stored), only the needed
transports allowed
.RB ( ext:: " and " file://
are refused), no submodule recursion, no LFS downloads during
checkout, protection against NTFS/HFS+ path aliases.
.IP \(bu 2
git runs in its own session without a controlling terminal and in its
own process group, with credential prompts disabled; nothing it spawns
can prompt on or write to the terminal, and the whole group is killed
on interruption or inactivity.
.IP \(bu 2
Text from servers and repositories is stripped of control characters
before it is printed, so escape sequences cannot reach the terminal.
.IP \(bu 2
HTTP requests are size\- and time\-limited and refuse redirects and
pagination links that leave the API host.
.PP
When browsing a working\-tree archive with your own git, consider
setting
.B safe.bareRepository=explicit
in your global git configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A repository failed, or the command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an archive of two GitHub owners, skipping forks:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir archive && cd archive
git\-archive \-\-skip\-forks https://github.com/termux https://github.com/sylirre
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update quietly from cron every night:
.PP
.RS
.nf
15 3 * * *  git\-archive \-C /srv/archive \-\-quiet
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop updating one repository, then check integrity and upstream drift:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git\-archive exclude termux/termux\-packages
git\-archive verify \-\-remote
.fi
.RE
.PP
Archive a self\-hosted GitLab group with a token:
.PP
.RS
.nf
MY_GL=glpat\-... git\-archive \-\-token\-env MY_GL https://git.example.org/group \e
    \-\-provider gitlab
.fi
.RE
